### Good Naming Examples

```typescript
// Components
auth-button.tsx → export const AuthButton
user-profile-card.tsx → export const UserProfileCard

// Hooks
use-auth.ts → export const useAuth
use-supabase-client.ts → export const useSupabaseClient

// Utilities
format-date.ts → export const formatDate
validate-email.ts → export const validateEmail

// Types
user.ts → export interface User
api-response.ts → export type ApiResponse

// Server Actions
actions.ts → export async function loginUser()

// Tests
auth-button.test.tsx
login.spec.ts (E2E)
```

## Project-Specific Conventions

### Next.js App Router

- Follow App Router conventions strictly
- Use proper special file names
- Keep route segments lowercase with dashes

### Supabase Integration

- Keep Supabase clients in `lib/supabase/`
- Use `client.ts` for client-side
- Use `server.ts` for server-side
- Use `types.ts` for database types

### Testing Files

- Use `.test.tsx` for Vitest/RTL tests
- Use `.spec.ts` for Playwright E2E tests
- Keep test files alongside source when possible
- Use `tests/` for E2E Playwright tests

### shadcn/ui Components

- Keep in `components/ui/`
- Don't rename shadcn/ui components
- Extend with wrapper components when needed
- Use kebab-case for file names

## Enforcement

- Use ESLint for code conventions
- Use Prettier for formatting
- Document conventions in README
- Review in pull requests
- Use consistent patterns across team
- Update conventions as project evolves
